    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0150" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg54"/>

                <head>No. 34.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Jay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 1,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 218.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch, No. 429, of the
                    8th ultimo, and to previous correspondence in regard to the World’s Exposition
                    to be held <pb facs="0151" n="55" xml:id="pg55"/> at Vienna in 1873, I have now
                    to state in reply that the subject has been presented to Congress, and now
                    awaits the action of that body.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
